BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Fascinating World of Fungi
DTSTART:20261001T000000
DTEND:20261001T000000
DTSTAMP:20260930T172235Z
UID:9c3817f84042fc5e7c72aa63dab9d9@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:From mushroom tattoos and T-shirt graphics to fungal-infused c
 offee\, gummies\, and nutritional supplements promising physical and spiri
 tual well-being\, fungi are having a cultural moment. Despite their growin
 g popularity\, fungi remain mysterious and misunderstood. Drawing from his
  new book\, The Complete Fungi: Evolution\, Diversity and Ecology (Princet
 on University Press\, 2026)\, David Hibbett will discuss the diversity of 
 fungi\, their impacts on human affairs\, and their roles in the evolution 
 of life on Earth. If you have ever wondered\, “What is a fungus?” or 
 “Why are there so many kinds of mushrooms?” this lecture is for you. N
 o prior knowledge or experience in mycology is required—just curiosity a
 bout the fascinating world of fungi. Copies of The Complete Fungi will be 
 available for purchase after the program. Supported by the Herman and Joan
  Suit Lecture Fund. Free event parking is available with registration. Par
 king will be available starting at 5pm at the 52 Oxford Street Garage. Reg
 ister by September 30 to receive parking registration instructions. Presen
 ted by the Harvard Museum of Natural History and the Harvard Museums of Sc
 ience & Culture in collaboration with the Boston Mycological Club. LEARN M
 ORE Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-
 fascinating-world-of-fungi/93293/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of No
 rthborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events
 .ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-fascinating-world-
 of-fungi/93293/
LOCATION:Geological Lecture Hall\, Geological Lecture Hall\, Harvard Museu
 m of the Ancient Near East 24 Oxford Street\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-fascinating-world-of-fungi/93293/
END:VEVENT
