UID:b1af5f3c00f1c8705dd703059c17fc@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:At this Meet the Artists event\, you'll connect with the exhib
 iting artists of Material Needs 2026 and learn more intimately how they ma
 de their collections come to life. Talk one-on-one with artists about thei
 r processes and experiences producing their work using Material Needs gran
 ts to support their cost of materials. Material Needs grants are made poss
 ible by the generosity of an anonymous ArtsWorcester donor. Exhibiting art
 ists and collections include: Ben Cline\, with woodworking boxes incorpora
 ting a new technique for the artist: stained glass Jennifer Davis Carey\, 
 with enamel works exploring the manifestations of female deities across di
 fferent cultures Kristi DiSalle\, with large-scale acrylic works consideri
 ng perimenopause's uncertain and isolating\, but rarely discussed\, biolog
 ical effects Kate Egnaczak\, with monotypes utilizing consumer waste colle
 cted from Worcester's Elm Park Claudio Eshun (AKA Don Claude)\, with Weste
 rn\, African\, and Afro-Descendant portraiture Anne Harris\, with drawings
 \, paintings\, and performance art videos in collaboration with vultures F
 ollowing your RSVP\, you are welcome to drop in anytime between 1:00 PM an
 d 3:00 PM that afternoon to chat with the exhibiting artists. The gallerie
 s will be open for normal hours until 5:00 PM\; you are welcome to stay un
 til then and continue browsing the exhibition by yourself\, or with a grou
 p. Light refreshments will be available at this free event. All are welcom
 e. Saturday\, October 3 // Drop in anytime between 1:00pm and 3:00pm ArtsW
 orcester // 44 Portland Street Worcester MA\, 01608 // RSVP by clicking he
 re. Parking is available at the Worcester Public Library (McGrath) Lot\, F
 ederal Plaza Garage\, Worcester Common Garage\, and Pearl-Elm Garage. Mete
 red street parking is also available. On weekends\, and on weekdays after 
 5:00 PM\, visitors may park in the Printers Building parking lot free of c
 harge. Please do not park in the lot across the street from the Printers B
 uilding\; you will be immediately towed. // Claudio Eshun (AKA Don Claude)
 \, Untitled (Auntie Elsie and Desdemona)\, digital inkjet print\, ed. 1/10
 \, 24" x 30"\, 2025 // Ben Cline\, Green\, red oak box with poplar splines
 \, green felt\, stained glass lid\, 5" x 9" x 5"\, 2025 // Jennifer Davis 
 Carey\, Persephone's Release\, vitreous enamel on copper assemblage\, 12" 
 x 8"\, 2026 // Kristi DiSalle\, Body Dysmorphia\, acrylic on canvas\, 36" 
 x 36"\, 2026 // Kate Egnaczak\, Blue Bottles\, acrylic gelli print\, 16" x
  20"\, 2026 // Sheila Papetti\, Hope\, coral velvet with white leather tri
 m\, 54" x 30" x 30"\, 2025 // Anne Harris\, I Heart Vultures\, colored pen
 cil on paper\, 10" x 10"\, 2026 Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Ev
 ent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/meet-the-artists%3a-mate
 rial-needs-2026/30892/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough
