BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raising Bilingual Children
DTSTART:20261003T000000
DTEND:20261003T000000
DTSTAMP:20260930T172235Z
UID:d80d7118bc4f6be44167c62d50395c@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Raising a bilingual or multilingual child is one of the greate
 st gifts you can give\, but it also comes with questions. How can I help m
 y child maintain our heritage language? What if they prefer English? Will 
 speaking more than one language confuse them? What does the research actua
 lly say? Join us at the Harvard Museum of Natural History for an engaging 
 morning designed specifically for parents\, caregivers\, and families rais
 ing bilingual children. Hear from leading researchers from Harvard and Tuf
 ts University as they share the latest findings on bilingualism\, heritage
  language development\, and practical strategies for supporting children
 ’s language growth at home. Each short talk will be followed by opportun
 ities for questions and discussion. You’ll leave with: Research-backed s
 trategies for raising bilingual and multilingual children Practical ideas 
 for supporting your heritage language in everyday life A better understand
 ing of the cognitive\, social\, cultural\, and educational benefits of bil
 ingualism Resources to help your family create a language-rich home Inspir
 ation and confidence to continue your bilingual journey $30/person for mem
 bers. $35/person for nonmembers. Price includes museum admission. Free eve
 nt parking is available with registration at the 52 Oxford Street Garage. 
 Not a member? Join today! Childcare (spaces are limited): While you attend
  the workshop\, your child can enjoy hands-on activities and gallery explo
 rations led by museum educators. Ages 3-12. Please note that children regi
 stered for childcare must be able to use a restroom independently. $15 per
  child LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://w
 ww.meetboston.com/event/raising-bilingual-children/93404/\n\nEvents Near M
 e: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback f
 rom massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/even
 t/raising-bilingual-children/93404/
LOCATION:Harvard Museum of Natural History\, Harvard Museum of Natural His
 tory 26 Oxford Street\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/raising-bilingual-children/93404/
END:VEVENT
