BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ivalas Quartet
DTSTART:20261004T000000
DTEND:20261004T000000
DTSTAMP:20260930T172235Z
UID:ace68aa4ea46e76ca93f54e1f27bce@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum presents the Ivalas Quarte
 t in their Weekend Concert Series. Franz Schubert's monumental “Death an
 d the Maiden” quartet anchors the Ivalas Quartet's program\, paired with
  two American works: an early piece in George Walker's "American" style (W
 alker died only a few years ago at age 96) and An Elegy: A Cry from the Gr
 ave\, a moving miniature by Carlos Simon\, whose Requiem for the Enslaved 
 had its Boston premiere at the Gardner Museum in 2022. Hailed by The Strad
  for playing with “tremendous heart and beauty\,” the Ivalas Quartet h
 as been changing the face of classical music since its inception in 2017 w
 ith a mission to enrich the classical music world by spotlighting past and
  present BIPOC composers alongside the standard repertory. The Isabella St
 ewart Gardner Museum’s Fall 2026 Weekend Concert Series features a ten-c
 oncert autumn season curated by Abrams Curator of Music George Steel held 
 on select Sundays from September 13 through November 22\, 2026. The fall s
 eason showcases world-class artists in the Museum’s extraordinary Calder
 wood Hall—a 300-seat “sonic cube” with three levels of balconies des
 igned so that 80% of seats are front row\, creating a uniquely intense and
  intentional listening experience. Dating to 1927\, the Gardner’s Weeken
 d Concert Series is the longest running museum music program in the countr
 y. Learn More/Get Tickets Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.mee
 tboston.com/event/ivalas-quartet/92814/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles
  of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-
 events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/ivalas-quartet/9
 2814/
LOCATION:Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum\, 25 Evans Way\, Boston\, MA\, 02
 115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/ivalas-quartet/92814/
END:VEVENT
