BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Contested Continent: The Struggle for North America\, c. 1000-1680
DTSTART:20261006T000000
DTEND:20261006T000000
DTSTAMP:20260930T172235Z
UID:8afd4a2883ab4a540d7c5bfb80f44c@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Distinguished historian Peter Mancall\, who is based at the Un
 iversity of Southern California\, discusses the sweeping history of North 
 America from the perspectives of its indigenous peoples and the earliest E
 uropeans to arrive on the continent. Drawing on his new book Contested Con
 tinent: The Struggle for North America\, c. 1000-1680 (June 2026)\, Mancal
 l underscores the titanic struggles between the peoples who had populated 
 the Americas for centuries and the migrants from the Old World who initiat
 ed changes that created a New World which offered boundless opportunities 
 for some and crushed the aspirations of others. This program will be held 
 both in person and livestreamed for a virtual audience. Register for both 
 options here. About Peter Mancall Peter C. Mancall is Distinguished Profes
 sor\, the Andrew W. Mellon Professor of the Humanities\, and the Linda and
  Harlan Martens Director of the USC-Huntington Early Modern Studies Instit
 ute at the University of Southern California. His book\, Contested Contine
 nt: The Struggle for North American\, c. 100-1680 \, the newest volume in 
 the acclaimed Oxford History of the United States series\, was published i
 n June 2026. Mancall is the author of numerous other books including Fatal
  Journey: The Final Expedition of Henry Hudson and Hakluyt's Promise: An E
 lizabethan's Obsession for an English America . His writings have appeared
  in the Smithsonian \, Time \, the Los Angeles Times \, and the Wall Stree
 t Journal \, among other outlets. He was elected to AAS membership in Octo
 ber 2008. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.
 discovercentralma.org/event/contested-continent%3a-the-struggle-for-north-
 america-c-1000-1680/30655/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northboro
