BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Songs of the Levant
DTSTART:20261006T000000
DTEND:20261006T000000
DTSTAMP:20260930T172235Z
UID:8eb249bb1341b7de8356c1b6bd685a@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Clark University welcomes musician\, composer\, and educator R
 amzi Aburedwan and Ensemble Dal’Ouna for an evening of music rooted in t
 he rich traditions of Palestine and the broader Levant. Featuring vocalist
  Mona Miari\, the ensemble demonstrates how musical practice can keep cult
 ural memory alive while continually reinventing it for the present. Abured
 wan’s own story gives this work particular resonance. Raised in the Al A
 mari refugee camp in the West Bank\, he discovered music in his youth and 
 went on to become a celebrated violist\, composer\, and educator. He is th
 e founder of Al-Kamandjâti\, an organization that provides music educatio
 n and performance opportunities to children and communities in Palestine a
 nd Palestinian refugee camps in Lebanon. His work has made music a vehicle
  for education\, cultural preservation\, community-building\, and creative
  possibility. Experience music that carries histories across borders\, con
 nects generations\, and asserts cultural presence in circumstances of disp
 lacement and conflict. Admission is free and open to the public. Sources: 
 Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.o
 rg/event/songs-of-the-levant/30928/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of 
 Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-even
 ts.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/songs-of-the-
 levant/30928/
LOCATION:Clark University\, Higgins Lounge\, Dana Commons\, 2nd Floor 36 M
 aywood Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 01603
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/songs-of-the-levant/30928/
END:VEVENT
